THE REAL BUG: Tests report TOTAL: 0/0 because harness calls 
window["a00_core"](TEST) but test files export runTests.

All 33 test files look like this:
  export async function runTests(TEST) {
    const tests = [], gs = TEST.getGS(), PERSIST = TEST.getPersist();
    async function test(name, fn) { try { await fn(); 
tests.push({name,status:"PASS"})} 
catch(e){tests.push({name,status:"FAIL",err:e.message})} }
    await test("test name", () => { if (!TEST.ok(expr)) throw new Error("fail");
});
    return tests;
  }

TEST methods: getGS(), getPersist(), ok(expr,msg), log(...)

WHAT TO DO:
1. Read tests/index.html
2. Find where test files are loaded and called (look for window[ or 
contentWindow[)
3. Replace with:
   a. After loadPromise resolves, capture GS and PERSIST from iframe:
        const GS_REF = { current: iframe.contentWindow.GS };
        const PERSIST_REF = { current: iframe.contentWindow.PERSIST };
   b. Create TEST object:
        const TEST = {
          getGS: () => GS_REF.current,
          getPersist: () => PERSIST_REF.current,
          ok: (expr, msg) => { if (!expr) throw new Error(msg||""); return true;
},
          log: (...a) => console.log("[TEST]", ...a),
        };
   c. For each test file, load via import() as ES module:
