    Fixed. Here's what changed:
    
    The bug: The old runSuite stripped export keywords then called window"a00_core" — but every test file exports runTests, not a file-name-keyed function.
    
    The fix: Rewrote runSuite (lines 107-194) to:
    1. Fetch the test file as text
    2. Grab GS and PERSIST from the iframe via ref objects
    3. Build a proper TEST object with getGS(), getPersist(), ok(), log() matching what test files expect
    4. Use iframe.contentWindow.eval() with a data-URI import() to run the code inside the iframe with GS/PERSIST in scope — avoids CORS entirely
    5. Call mod.runTests(T) and collect the returned [{name, status, ...}] array
    
    Results are reported via postMessage back to the harness, which tallies them properly into TOTAL: N/N.
    
    Committed and pushed to squad/test-iframe-fix. Syntax checked clean.
